- id: '2095962962808746380'
  text: 'GPT-6 Astra on my NYC test. Astra high in Codex. Opus 5 underneath.


    Its fast. Under 20 minutes to finish.


    Not as eager as Opus or Fable to go outside the scope. I had to send a follow
    up prompt just to add camera movement.


    Generally good, probably more detail than Opus on the initial pass, but it forgets
    things. With Opus I could physically zoom into the bridges and see cars.


    This is a massive leap from GPT-5.6 Sol though, which was rough on this prompt.


    I use time as an effort measure. If it finishes in 20 minutes I dont feel it put
    enough into iterating and improving. The faster the model gets, the longer I want
    to force it into a 50 minute loop.


    Overall good. I just feel a lot more detail and effort could have gone in than
    one shot.'
